Description: Revert the device and apply the layout on the GUI thread
 ChoicePage ran PartitionCoreModule::revertDevice() (and revertAllDevices())
 on a worker thread under a ScanningDialog, in the device choice, in every
 install choice, and in "Replace a partition" before laying out the new
 partitions. revertDevice() rescans the device, deletes the old Device and
 re-initializes the PartitionModel and the BootLoaderModel, while the GUI
 thread's preview views paint from those models. In "Replace a partition" with encryption checked, choosing
 the free space and then confirming the passphrase reverts the device in that
 worker, and Calamares crashed with a segfault in PartitionModel::data()
 (Lenovo Legion Pro 7, 2026-10-13; in QEMU, confirming the passphrase again
 and again after choosing the space crashed it on the third round, "segfault
 at 0 ... in libcalamares_viewmodule_partition.so[8a38d]", which addr2line
 resolves to PartitionModel::data). Choosing the space after confirming the
 passphrase did not crash, because nothing had changed the device yet, so
 nothing was reverted.
 .
 The patch runs those reverts, and the replace step's layout, on the GUI
 thread, in the order the worker and its continuation ran them. Reverting is a
 rescan of the chosen device and the layout is in-memory, so the page pauses
 briefly instead of showing the scanning dialog. Applies on top of
 replace-read-selection-before-revert.patch.
